{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01W7", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-projective-is-quasi-projective-proper}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0e9c1ade90b92f700ef5e50691e265c4a037e58eb0d638fbfeef55a951ca0804", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7c9323236ee5054e81afe3a7cc77de196a27b007de54e723dbebf0d1929fa6b7", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a morphism of schemes. Then\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0003> is projective if and only if <MATH_0004> is quasi-projective and proper, and\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0005> is H-projective if and only if <MATH_0006> is H-quasi-projective and proper.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:20bfa01c06507927bca71f254f014680201d22f1d08241f73afaa74610825edd", "unit_id": "tag:0BCL:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01W7", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$X \\to S$", "MATH_0004": "$X \\to X'$", "MATH_0005": "$X' \\to S$", "MATH_0006": "$X \\to S$", "MATH_0007": "$X$", "MATH_0008": "$X'$", "MATH_0009": "$X \\to X'$", "MATH_0010": "$X'$", "MATH_0011": "$S$", "MATH_0012": "$X$", "MATH_0013": "$X \\to S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-projective-quasi-projective}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-locally-projective-proper}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-projective-open-projective}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-image-proper-scheme-closed}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{definition-projective}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{lemma-H-projective}", "REF_0007": "\\ref{lemma-H-quasi-projective-open-H-projective}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:261f5a36d5c211771b430f3ccd0e3aa12e1dbec68687a44f824633a4280c90b7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d535e66d424a3f18fb70418300c9ee072848108961dfa04b44fae6368a2c6a35", "source_text": "If <MATH_0001> is projective, then <MATH_0002> is quasi-projective by\nLemma <REF_0001> and proper by\nLemma <REF_0002>. Conversely, if\n<MATH_0003> is quasi-projective and proper, then we can choose\nan open immersion <MATH_0004> with <MATH_0005> projective by\nLemma <REF_0003>.\nSince <MATH_0006> is proper, we see that <MATH_0007> is closed in <MATH_0008>\n(Lemma <REF_0004>), i.e.,\n<MATH_0009> is a (open and) closed immersion.\nSince <MATH_0010> is isomorphic to a closed subscheme of a projective\nbundle over <MATH_0011> (Definition <REF_0005>)\nwe see that the same thing is true for <MATH_0012>, i.e.,\n<MATH_0013> is a projective morphism. This proves (1).\nThe proof of (2) is the same, except it uses\nLemmas <REF_0006> and\n<REF_0007>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3f02fcc2fe2cf77b72bfdfa73cc64074c977048ca8fe8f7888e8f714169fbd43", "unit_id": "tag:0BCL:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01W7", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$g : Y \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$g$", "MATH_0006": "$g \\circ f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-composition-projective}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7f5719362501081abba8adf1d1230ac8ab6267d053f5f64e24c44590c804c71b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3711b555902a8afb4e2b4db43cd86bb3bcd446da53f196d3791a451e261faa90", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> be morphisms of schemes.\nIf <MATH_0003> is quasi-compact and quasi-separated and <MATH_0004> and <MATH_0005> are projective,\nthen <MATH_0006> is projective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e9610d83f75ec415e01322ac8a6aa89549608f11d8383c9ffddc31562c54c30d", "unit_id": "tag:0C4P:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01W7", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$g$", "MATH_0003": "$g \\circ f$", "MATH_0004": "$g \\circ f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-projective-quasi-projective}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-locally-projective-proper}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-composition-proper}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-composition-quasi-projective}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-projective-is-quasi-projective-proper}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:60b6c32e422181ae6b84739bcefd22af2a0925ecbf5c5985b36bdae577406f98", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a2a82451f3655edb5f7787a472dd4bf299e0b04e7c04c25bd01cf1dbd3accbd8", "source_text": "By Lemmas <REF_0001> and\n<REF_0002>\nwe see that <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> are quasi-projective and proper.\nBy Lemmas <REF_0003> and\n<REF_0004>\nwe see that <MATH_0003> is proper and quasi-projective.\nThus <MATH_0004> is projective by\nLemma <REF_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0a5dc04217a751d1a74f0eef72792dfa41676ab3274e86cb33c128e0c7768984", "unit_id": "tag:0C4P:proof"}
